WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:05.800
When a ride opens a new map, Results celebrates it.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.035
A gold card names the map, says where it rides, and offers to ride it: Neon

00:00:15.035 --> 00:00:16.466
Docklands is open.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.260
It is the one moment the app moves. The card fades in and grows, then its photo

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:32.000
comes into colour. With reduced motion, it only fades.

00:00:38.714 --> 00:00:44.415
The backend decides. A top three finish against bots opens the next map, stars open

00:00:44.415 --> 00:00:48.973
another, and level ten opens Vice City. It names the map once.

00:00:54.199 --> 00:00:56.550
When nothing opened, there is no card.

00:01:04.523 --> 00:01:09.060
On a phone the card leads what you earned, below the standings. From a tablet in

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:11.118
landscape, it sits beside them.

00:01:17.428 --> 00:01:22.248
What the tests prove: every unlock rule, the answer through the API, and the card

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:23.441
and its motion.

00:01:27.751 --> 00:01:32.355
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:37.212
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:37.212 --> 00:01:38.883
every hill and interval.

00:01:39.228 --> 00:01:44.406
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:44.406 --> 00:01:49.854
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:49.854 --> 00:01:52.844
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:53.189 --> 00:01:55.682
A custom workout lives under Profile.
